    "description": "HMD initially used a single-digit numbering system (1-9) to denote market tier, with decimal suffixes (.1, .2) for refreshes and 'Plus' for enhanced variants. It later transitioned to a letter-number system (C, G, X, XR) to clearly segment Entry, Budget, Mid-range, and Rugged categories. Recently, under the standalone HMD brand, it has shifted to evocative single-word names (Pulse, Skyline, Fusion, Crest, Arc, Aura, Luma, Ivalo, Key) often supplemented by 'Pro', 'Max', or '5G' suffixes to denote higher-tier variants within the series."
